    "result": "Perfect! All tests pass now. The two issues were:\n\n1. **Governance test**: I added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` to the governance module's `index.js` so the test can import `APPROVAL_STATUSES`.\n\n2. **Toxicity metric**: I fixed the `toxicityMetric` function signature to only accept `outputs` (removing the `bannedTerms` parameter). The issue was that `runEvaluations` was calling it with `(outputs, references)`, which caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging all outputs as toxic.\n\nThe full frai-core test suite (28 tests across 8 test files) is now passing.",
